# Shell scripts, container entrypoints and service units must be LF on disk:
# a CRLF checkout gives `sh` a "\r" in `set -u\r` and gives the kernel a
# shebang it cannot resolve ("exec ./entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory").
# core.autocrlf=true is common on Windows, so pin these by path rather than
# trusting the clone.
* text=auto
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
